>how do I "call the scroll ______", what do I name which? 

I don't quite understand the question. Some scrolls (and potions, etc.) will 
prompt you for a name the first time you use them. If you can tell, from the 
message given when you use the item, what kind of item it is, this is a handy 
way to identify the item for the next time you run into one like it. The
process of associating messages with items is one you just have to learn over
time, I'm afraid, although most of them DO make sense, if only in hindsight...

Of course, you can name items anytime you want, if you have at least one of 
them in your possession. A name given to a SPECIFIC object is just a tag for 
that object. You might want to tag something as being "cursed" or "out of 
charges", for instance. You can also name items NON-specifically, which 
attaches that name to the whole object class. So, for instance, if you figure
out that e.g. a platinum wand is a wand of fire, you can name it "fire", and
every time you find a platinum wand, it'll say "wand named fire". Convenient.

