I find that Barbarians or Samurais are best if all you want to do is hack 'n' 
slash. Slightly less so for Valkyries or Cavemen. Tourists, Healers, Rogues & 
Wizards tend to suck in that regard. Priests and Knights are mediocre. For a 
beginner, I'd stick with the physically-tough classes until you get the 
"feel" for ordinary combat situations. Then, from there, you can branch off 
into whatever magic-using/special-ability/special-strategy class(es) take 
your fancy. Each player class has its strengths and weaknesses, but some take 
longer to learn how to play to their maximum potential. Personally, I just do 
random picks, since I enjoy variety...

